{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["And the reason for <b>\"and he saw the Kenite\"</b> is likewise that he saw their land, for he was dwelling among Amalek (I Samuel 15:6). <b>\"And he took up his parable and said\"</b> to them by way of counsel: <b>\"Eitan is your dwelling, and set your nest in the rock\"</b> — that is, set your dwelling in an enduring place and in the rock, that you may turn aside and come down from among Amalek lest you be destroyed with him, and set your dwelling in an enduring rock with Israel, as it says: \"And the descendants of the Kenite, the father-in-law of Moses, went up from the city of palms with the descendants of Judah\" (Judges 1:16). And he said: <b>\"For if Kain be for destroying\"</b> — that is, do not fear coming among Israel, for even if you are destroyed together with them, for as they go into exile for Israel they will clear the land of its inhabitants; <b>\"until what point shall Asshur carry you captive\"</b> — he will never carry you captive, for you will be redeemed from his hand together with Israel. And if you remain with Amalek, your end shall be utter destruction with them. And likewise \"until what point, YHWH, will You be angry forever\" (Psalms 79:5), \"until what point will my glory be for shame\" (ibid. 4:2), like \"until when\"; or it may mean that it reaches a great magnitude, as in \"how deep is your heart\" (Ezekiel 16:30), \"what was your mother? A lioness\" (ibid. 19:2) — meaning, to what great and exalted height the captivity that Asshur carries you off to will ascend — it is accounted as nothing to you, for you will not perish as you would have perished with Amalek. Therefore he took up his parable concerning Asshur, that a time will come for his land as well, and there is none who will escape on the great and awesome day of YHWH against all the nations, when ships shall come from the hand of Kittim, and they are the Romans, and they shall afflict Asshur that is mentioned here, and they shall afflict Eber, which is Israel, meaning that they shall afflict both the exiles and the inhabitants, and he too is a people of Kittim, utterly destroyed in the end.\nAnd behold, he concluded his words with the destruction of Kittim, for they are the fourth beast that shall be cut off at the hand of the Messiah, as it is said: \"I was beholding then because of the voice of the great words which the horn spoke; I beheld even until the beast was slain, and its body destroyed, and given to be burned with fire\" (Daniel 7:11), for \"utter destruction\" (עדי אובד) — the cutting off of their seed entirely. And this is well known from the words of our Sages, that the fourth beast that Daniel saw is Rome, which exiled us, and it is that which shall perish at the hand of the Messiah. And do not wonder at this because the third kingdom is Greece, as is explicit there in Daniel (Daniel 8:21), for Kittim is of the seed of Greece, as it is said: \"And the sons of Javan: Elishah and Tarshish, Kittim and Dodanim\" (Genesis 10:4). For this is true and our Sages concede it, as they said (Babylonian Talmud, Megillah 6a): \"Italy of Greece — this is the great city of Rome.\" And it is well known that the name of the land of which Rome is a part is called in their books and in their language Italia. But the matter is just as with Canaan, for the Jebusite and the Amorite and the Girgashite and the Hivite are his sons, and they and their father are each reckoned as a nation unto itself, as it is said: \"the Hittite and the Girgashite and the Amorite and the Canaanite and the Perizzite and the Hivite and the Jebusite, seven nations greater and mightier than you\" (Deuteronomy 7:1). And so it was because each one of these sons had become a mighty nation, and those nations were called by the name of their father, while the rest of the sons of Canaan who were not as mighty as their brothers were traced back to him. And likewise the land of Egypt is traced to the father, while the Philistines and the Caphtorim are sons belonging to other peoples. And so too with the families mentioned in the portion of Pinchas: \"of Machir, the family of the Machirite; and Machir begot Gilead; of Gilead, the family of the Gileadite\" (Numbers 26:29), and so many others. So too here, the sons of Javan, Elishah and Tarshish, were traced to Javan, and they are the third kingdom, while Kittim had become a mighty nation and is reckoned as the fourth kingdom, and it is the one whose kingdom will endure until the Messiah and will perish by his hand.\nAnd Rabbi Abraham was confused in this matter and inserted among them the kingdom of Ishmael, for their dread fell upon him, and he argued: how could a kingdom as great and mighty as that not be reckoned? But this argument stems from a lack of understanding, for the four kingdoms that Daniel saw all stand one after the other, each one conquering the preceding and seizing dominion from it, and each one imposing servitude and exile upon Israel during the days of its rule. Therefore Daniel was shown in his dream that the Chaldeans would enslave us, and afterward the Persians would seize dominion and enslave us, and after them in their place the Greeks, and afterward the Romans would prevail and seize dominion and enslave us until the time of the end, for their kingdom will not cease except at the hand of the Redeemer. Now our exile coincides with the days of the four kingdoms, but if other kingdoms exist in the world during the days of these four, Scripture does not reckon them, and Daniel did not see them, and he has no need at all to see them for knowledge of the redemption. And behold, in the days of Persia and Greece, and even today, there are kingdoms greater than Rome and Ishmael besides, such as the people of India and Cush and Baghdad and Romania and the Tatar and others, and afterward many more kingdoms will be reckoned. And it is well known that Rome exiled us in the days of Vespasian and Titus, not the Ishmaelites; therefore wherever we are, whether under Ishmael or from India even to Cush, we are in the exile of Rome until its memory shall perish and we shall be redeemed from it. And who knows — perhaps the kingdom of Ishmael will yet perish before the Messiah.\nBut the fourth beast is that which exiled us, as it says of it: \"that horn made war with the holy ones and prevailed against them\" (Daniel 7:21). And it imposes exile upon us until the Messiah, as it is written: \"until the Ancient of Days came, and judgment was given to the holy ones of the Most High, and the time arrived, and the kingship was held by the holy ones\" (Daniel 7:22). And everyone who understands the visions of Daniel will find this explicit there, for in the second vision he saw the ram that pushes, and it was explained to him that it is the kingdom of Persia, and the shaggy goat is the king of Greece, and the great horn is the first king, Alexander, who conquered Persia. And when he is strong his kingdom will be broken and four will stand under it — they are his four generals who rule under him after his death. And Scripture mentioned: \"And from one of them came forth a little horn, which grew exceedingly toward the south and toward the east and toward the beautiful land\" (Daniel 8:9), and said of it: \"and it grew great even to the prince of the host, and from it the daily offering was taken away\" (Daniel 8:11). And behold, this clearly refers to the kingdom of Rome, which comes forth from Greece, for it is one of its sons, and it is the one that removes the daily offering. Therefore they both appeared to him as one beast, namely the shaggy goat, one of whose horns grew and removed the daily offering. And there are further proofs there to this effect. And the tradition of our Sages is truth; it requires no reinforcement."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {0 "The Hebrew text interleaves two paragraph-like blocks within a single comment (marked by <br> tags); these are preserved as paragraph breaks. Place-name identifications such as Bagdad, Romania, and the Tatar are rendered as they appear in the Hebrew, reflecting medieval geographical terminology."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:09:07.437798660Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}